    "result": {
      "answer": "Here's a full overview of the 15 registered pipelines and the best fit for a **FASTA annotation task**.\n\n---\n\n## Available Pipelines\n\n### Public pipelines (production-ready)\n\n| Pipeline | Engine | Accepts FASTA? | Best for… |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Antimicrobial resistance detection** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` + FASTQ | AMR gene candidates from contigs/reads |\n| **Bacterial functional annotation** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` + FASTQ | Gene function / orthology from bacteria |\n| **Bacterial genome annotation** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` only | **★ Gene & feature annotation of assembled bacterial contigs** |\n| **Bacterial genome mutation analysis** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` + `.fas` | SNP calling / phylogeny from assembled genomes |\n| **Bacterial read variant analysis** | shell | FASTQ only (no bare FASTA) | Read-based variant calling |\n| **Bacterial virulence-factor detection** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` + FASTQ | Virulence-factor sequence candidates |\n| **Metagenomic de novo assembly** | WDL | FASTQ only | Assembly from metagenomic reads |\n| **Metagenomic pathogen identification** | WDL | FASTQ only | Pathogen detection from host-filtered reads |\n| **Metagenomic read quality control** | WDL | FASTQ only | Read QC / host removal |\n| **Pathogen variant risk assessment** | WDL | FASTQ only | Variant calling + risk report (H1N1, H3N2, SARS-CoV-2) |\n| **RNA secondary-structure prediction** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` | MFE structure prediction for RNA/DNA sequences |\n| **Viral genome mutation analysis** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` | SNP calling / phylogeny from viral genomes |\n| **Viral molecular typing** | WDL | FASTQ only | Influenza/SARS-CoV-2 typing via Nextclade |\n\n### Internal pipelines (educational demonstrations)\n\n| Pipeline | Engine | Accepts FASTA? | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **DNA analysis template** | shell | `.fasta/.fa/.fna` | Demo only, not validated |\n| **Nextflow pipeline template** | nextflow | `.fa/.fasta/.fna` | Nextflow engine demo |\n| **Shell metadata assignment template** | shell | `.fasta/.fa` + `.txt` | Metadata join demo |\n| **Snakemake pipeline template** | snakemake | `.fa/.fasta/.fna` | Snakemake engine demo |\n| **WDL pipeline template** | WDL | `.fa/.fasta/.fna` | WDL engine demo |\n\n---\n\n## Best Fit: **Bacterial genome annotation**\n\nFor a general FASTA annotation task—taking assembled nucleotide contigs and producing gene features, protein translations, and functional labels—this pipeline is the clear choice.\n\n### Required input\n\n| Input | Format | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `genome` | Single FASTA file (`.fasta`, `.fa`, `.fna`) | Assembled bacterial contigs |\n\n### Example staged data\n\n2 synthetic contigs (660 bytes total):\n\n```\n>mock_contig_1 synthetic_example_length_264\nATGAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTTAG\nATGAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTAAACCCGGGTTTTAG\n...\n>mock_contig_2 synthetic_example_length_300\nATGCGTACGTTAGCTAGCTAGGCTAACCGGTTACGATCGATGCTAGCTAGCTAACGTTAGCGGATCCGATGCTAA\n...\n```\n\n### Outputs\n\n| Artifact | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `gff` | Gene feature annotations (GFF3) |\n| `genbank` | GenBank flat-file format |\n| `features` | Feature table |\n| `proteins` | Translated protein sequences (FASTA) |\n| `genes` | Nucleotide gene sequences (FASTA) |\n| `contigs` | Original input (copy) |\n| `hypotheticals` | Hypothetical protein sequences |\n| `bakta_json` | Bakta-format JSON (if Bakta used) |\n| `inference` | Annotation inference provenance |\n| `report` | Human-readable annotation report |\n| `metrics` | Quality metrics |\n| `plot_png` / `plot_svg` | Annotation summary figures |\n| `summary` | Tabular summary |\n| `bundle` | Raw archived tool output |\n| `log` | Pipeline log |\n\n### Key parameters\n\n| Parameter | Default | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `annotator` | `prokka` | Also supports `bakta` |\n| `prefix` | `annotation` | Output filename prefix |\n| `genus` / `species` / `strain` | empty | Optional organism metadata |\n| `translation_table` | 11 | Bacterial genetic code |\n| `gram` | `?` | Gram sign (`+` / `-` / `?`) |\n| `cpus` | 1 | Thread count |\n| `complete` | false | Set `true` for complete circular genomes |\n| `rfam` | false | Include ncRNA via Rfam |\n| `compliant` | false | Force GenBank-compliant features |\n\n### Limitations\n\n- **Bacterial only** — this pipeline uses Prokka/Bakta which are designed for bacterial genomes. For viral or eukaryotic FASTA annotation, consider `viral_genome_mutation_analysis` (variant-focused) or use the general sequence tools (`sequence_find_orfs`, `sequence_translate`) directly.\n- **Assembled contigs required** — raw reads must first be assembled; for that, use `metagenomic_de_novo_assembly` (with the caveat that it prefers FASTQ input).\n- **Annotation quality** depends on the selected tool (`prokka` vs `bakta`) and database versions.\n- **No taxonomy or abundance** — this is purely structural/functional annotation, not metagenomic profiling.\n\n---\n\n### Other FASTA-compatible alternatives worth noting\n\n- **Bacterial functional annotation** — if you need functional term assignments (e.g. KEGG/COG) rather than full structural gene annotation, this is the complementary option.\n- **RNA secondary-structure prediction** — if your FASTA contains RNA or DNA sequences for structure prediction rather than gene annotation.\n- **Antimicrobial resistance detection** / **Virulence-factor detection** — if your annotation goal is specifically to find resistance or virulence genes in the FASTA.\n\nWould you like me to stage the example data and walk through a full plan for the **bacterial genome annotation** pipeline, or explore one of the other options?",
